IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 12 Division 2 (the general penalty, the default penalty, proceedings, composition),
-- and the First Schedule. Part agent sgo.
-- This module is called by the offence provisions of every part: s 407(2) is the penalty where the Act names none, s 408 is the
-- default penalty, s 408(3) is "an officer who is in default". The offence provisions of Part 12 themselves are in sgo-offences.l4.
--
-- READING A RESULT. A function answers JUST TRUE (yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) or NOTHING (the text does not
-- say). An unmet element of an offence answers NOTHING (fork register, site type (i)). Money is Singapore dollars.

§ `Section 407: the general penalty provisions`

§§ `Section 407(1): who is guilty of an offence`

-- src:28072 | 407.—(1) A person who —
-- src:28074 | (a) does that which under this Act the person is forbidden to
-- src:28075 | do;
-- src:28077 | (b) does not do that which under this Act the person is required
-- src:28078 | or directed to do; or
-- src:28080 | (c) otherwise contravenes or fails to comply with any
-- src:28081 | provision of this Act,
-- src:28083 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 407(1) (src:28072-28083)
GIVEN `the person does that which under this Act the person is forbidden to do` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not do that which under this Act the person is required or directed to do` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person otherwise contravenes or fails to comply with a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 407(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `the person does that which under this Act the person is forbidden to do`
       OR `the person does not do that which under this Act the person is required or directed to do`
       OR `the person otherwise contravenes or fails to comply with a provision of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "A person who (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ... shall be guilty of an offence" says nothing of a person who does none of the three; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

§§ `Section 407(2): the penalty where the Act states none`

-- src:28085 | (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under this Act shall be
-- src:28086 | liable on conviction to a penalty or punishment not exceeding the
-- src:28087 | penalty or punishment expressly mentioned as the penalty or
-- src:28088 | punishment for the offence, or if a penalty or punishment is not so
-- src:28089 | mentioned, to a fine not exceeding $1,000.
@ref s 407(2) (src:28085-28089)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the penalty or punishment the Act expressly mentions as the penalty or punishment for the offence` IS A MAYBE Penalty
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 407(2) the highest penalty or punishment on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under this Act`
    THEN JUST (CONSIDER `the penalty or punishment the Act expressly mentions as the penalty or punishment for the offence`
               WHEN JUST expressed THEN expressed
               WHEN NOTHING THEN Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)   -- "if a penalty or punishment is not so mentioned, to a fine not exceeding $1,000"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection fixes the penalty of "a person who is guilty of an offence under this Act" and says nothing of a person who is not

§§ `Section 407(3) and (4): serving a summons`

-- The three ways of service the subsection names. The list is not closed ("may ... be served"), so any other way answers NOTHING.
DECLARE `s 407(3) way of serving a summons` IS ONE OF
    `s 407(3)(a) delivering it to that person`
    `s 407(3)(b) delivering it to an adult person residing at that person's last known place of abode or employed at that person's last known place of business`
    `s 407(3)(c) forwarding it by registered post in a cover addressed to that person at the person's last known place of abode or business or at any address furnished by the person`
    `s 407(3) some other way`

-- src:28091 | (3) Every summons issued for an offence committed by an officer
-- src:28092 | of a company or other person under this Act or any regulations may,
-- src:28093 | despite anything in this Act, be served —
-- src:28095 | (a) by delivering it to that person;
-- src:28097 | (b) by delivering it to any adult person residing at that person’s
-- src:28098 | last known place of abode or employed at that person’s last
-- src:28099 | known place of business; or
-- src:28101 | (c) by forwarding it by registered post in a cover addressed to
-- src:28102 | that person at the person’s last known place of abode or
-- src:28103 | business or at any address furnished by the person.
@ref s 407(3) (src:28091-28103)
GIVEN `the summons is issued for an offence committed by an officer of a company or other person under this Act or any regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `s 407(3) way of serving a summons`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 407(3) the summons may be served in that way` MEANS
    IF NOT `the summons is issued for an offence committed by an officer of a company or other person under this Act or any regulations`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every summons issued for an offence committed by an officer of a company or other person under this Act or any regulations"
    ELSE CONSIDER way
         WHEN `s 407(3)(a) delivering it to that person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 407(3)(b) delivering it to an adult person residing at that person's last known place of abode or employed at that person's last known place of business` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 407(3)(c) forwarding it by registered post in a cover addressed to that person at the person's last known place of abode or business or at any address furnished by the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may, despite anything in this Act, be served" lists three ways and does not say "only"

-- src:28105 | (4) In proving service by registered post, it is sufficient to prove that
-- src:28106 | the registered cover containing the summons was duly addressed and
-- src:28107 | posted.
@ref s 407(4) (src:28105-28107)
GIVEN `the registered cover containing the summons was duly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registered cover containing the summons was duly posted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 407(4) service by registered post is sufficiently proved` MEANS
    IF `the registered cover containing the summons was duly addressed` AND `the registered cover containing the summons was duly posted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is sufficient to prove that the registered cover ... was duly addressed and posted" says what suffices, not that anything less fails

§ `Section 408: default penalties`

§§ `Section 408(1): the further offence and the additional daily penalty`

-- src:28114 | 408.—(1) Where a default penalty is provided in any section of this
-- src:28115 | Act, any person who is convicted of an offence under this Act or who
-- src:28116 | has been dealt with under section 409B for an offence under this Act
-- src:28117 | in relation to that section shall be guilty of a further offence under this
-- src:28118 | Act if the offence continues after the person is so convicted or after
-- src:28119 | the person has been so dealt with and liable to an additional penalty
-- src:28120 | for each day during which the offence so continues of not more than
-- src:28121 | the amount expressed in the section as the amount of the default
-- src:28122 | penalty or, if an amount is not so expressed, of not more than $200.
@ref s 408(1) (src:28114-28122)
GIVEN `a default penalty is provided in the section of this Act under which the offence arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been convicted of an offence under this Act in relation to that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been dealt with under section 409B for an offence under this Act in relation to that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence continues after the person is so convicted or after the person has been so dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 408(1) the person is guilty of a further offence` MEANS
    IF    `a default penalty is provided in the section of this Act under which the offence arises`
       AND (   `the person has been convicted of an offence under this Act in relation to that section`
            OR `the person has been dealt with under section 409B for an offence under this Act in relation to that section`)
       AND `the offence continues after the person is so convicted or after the person has been so dealt with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Where a default penalty is provided in any section ... shall be guilty of a further offence ... if the offence continues" says nothing of the person for whom an element fails; unmet element of an offence (split site type (i))

-- The most the person is liable to for each day: "not more than the amount expressed in the section as the amount of the default penalty or,
-- if an amount is not so expressed, of not more than $200."
@ref s 408(1) (src:28114-28122)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of a further offence under section 408(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the section expresses as the amount of the default penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 408(1) the highest additional penalty for each day during which the offence continues` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of a further offence under section 408(1)`
    THEN JUST (CONSIDER `the amount the section expresses as the amount of the default penalty, in Singapore dollars`
               WHEN JUST expressed THEN expressed
               WHEN NOTHING THEN 200)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the additional penalty is that of a person who "shall be guilty of a further offence"

@ref s 408(1) (src:28114-28122)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of a further offence under section 408(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the section expresses as the amount of the default penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the number of days during which the offence has continued after the person was so convicted or so dealt with` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 408(1) the highest total additional penalty for the days the offence has continued` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 408(1) the highest additional penalty for each day during which the offence continues` `the person is guilty of a further offence under section 408(1)` `the amount the section expresses as the amount of the default penalty, in Singapore dollars`
    WHEN JUST perDay THEN JUST (perDay TIMES `the number of days during which the offence has continued after the person was so convicted or so dealt with`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The seam the keel asks of this section (PLAN.md section 4, table A): s 4(1) "default penalty" means "a default penalty within the meaning of section 408".
-- A penalty is a default penalty within the meaning of s 408 where it is the additional penalty for each day that s 408(1) describes.
@ref s 408(1) (src:28114-28122)
GIVEN `the penalty is the additional penalty for each day during which an offence continues, that a section of this Act provides as a default penalty and section 408(1) imposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 408(1) the penalty is a default penalty within the meaning of section 408` MEANS
    `the penalty is the additional penalty for each day during which an offence continues, that a section of this Act provides as a default penalty and section 408(1) imposes`

-- The further offence as a prohibition: derived from the flat statement that the person "shall be guilty of a further offence".
DECLARE `s 408(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 408(1) let the offence continue after the conviction or composition`

@ref s 408(1) (src:28114-28122)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 408(1) act`
`s 408(1) a person convicted or dealt with must not let the offence continue` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 408(1) let the offence continue after the conviction or composition`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the offence continued after the person was convicted or dealt with under section 409B"

§§ `Section 408(2): an offence for something not done in time continues until it is done`

-- src:28129 | (2) Where any offence is committed by a person by reason of the
-- src:28130 | person’s failure to comply with any provision of this Act under which
-- src:28131 | the person is required or directed to do anything within a particular
-- src:28132 | period, that offence, for the purposes of subsection (1), is deemed to
-- src:28133 | continue so long as the thing so required or directed to be done by the
-- src:28134 | person remains undone, even though such period has elapsed.
@ref s 408(2) (src:28129-28134)
GIVEN `the offence is committed by reason of the person's failure to comply with a provision of this Act under which the person is required or directed to do anything within a particular period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing so required or directed to be done by the person remains undone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 408(2) the offence is deemed to continue` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offence is committed by reason of the person's failure to comply with a provision of this Act under which the person is required or directed to do anything within a particular period`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where any offence is committed by a person by reason of the person's failure to comply with any provision of this Act under which the person is required or directed to do anything within a particular period"
    ELSE (IF `the thing so required or directed to be done by the person remains undone`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to continue so long as the thing so required or directed to be done by the person remains undone"

§§ `Section 408(3): an officer who is in default`

-- src:28136 | (3) For the purposes of any provision of this Act which provides
-- src:28137 | that an officer of a company or corporation who is in default is guilty
-- src:28138 | of an offence under this Act or is liable to a penalty or punishment, the
-- src:28139 | phrase “officer who is in default” or any like phrase means any officer
-- src:28140 | of the company or corporation who knowingly and wilfully —
-- src:28142 | (a) is guilty of the offence; or
-- src:28144 | (b) authorises or permits the commission of the offence.
@ref s 408(3) (src:28136-28144)
GIVEN `the officer is guilty of the offence knowingly and wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 408(3) the officer is an officer who is in default` MEANS
    IF    `the officer is guilty of the offence knowingly and wilfully`
       OR `the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the commission of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the phrase \"officer who is in default\" or any like phrase means any officer of the company or corporation who knowingly and wilfully (a) is guilty of the offence; or (b) authorises or permits the commission of the offence" (a definition that says "means")

§ `Section 409: proceedings how and when taken`

§§ `Section 409(1): who may take proceedings`

DECLARE `s 409(1) who takes the proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `s 409(1) the Registrar`
    `s 409(1) a person other than the Registrar`

-- Fork (NOTES F-409-1): the authorisation of the Public Prosecutor is read as governing both limbs, because the text puts it before
-- "be taken by the Registrar or with the written consent of the Minister by any person".
-- src:28148 | 409.—(1) Except where provision is otherwise made in this Act,
-- src:28149 | proceedings for any offence under this Act may, with the
-- src:28150 | authorisation of the Public Prosecutor, be taken by the Registrar or
-- src:28151 | with the written consent of the Minister by any person.
@ref s 409(1) (src:28148-28151)
GIVEN `the Act makes other provision for the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who takes the proceedings` IS A `s 409(1) who takes the proceedings`
      `the Public Prosecutor has authorised the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409(1) the person may take proceedings for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the Act makes other provision for the proceedings`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where provision is otherwise made in this Act" hands the case to the provision that makes it
    ELSE (IF NOT `the Public Prosecutor has authorised the proceedings`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, with the authorisation of the Public Prosecutor, be taken" is a grant limited by the authorisation; it does not say "only"
          ELSE CONSIDER `the person who takes the proceedings`
               WHEN `s 409(1) the Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
               WHEN `s 409(1) a person other than the Registrar` THEN
                   (IF `the Minister has consented in writing`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the written consent of the Minister by any person"

§§ `Section 409(3): which court`

-- "other than an offence punishable with imprisonment for a term exceeding 6 months": the Magistrate's Court. "of 6 months or more": the District Court.
-- An offence punishable with exactly 6 months falls within both (finding in NOTES.md).
-- src:28157 | (3) Proceedings for any offence under this Act, other than an
-- src:28158 | offence punishable with imprisonment for a term exceeding
-- src:28159 | 6 months, may be prosecuted in a Magistrate’s Court and in the
-- src:28160 | case of an offence punishable with imprisonment for a term of
-- src:28161 | 6 months or more may be prosecuted in a District Court.
@ref s 409(3) (src:28157-28161)
GIVEN `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409(3) the proceedings may be prosecuted in a Magistrate's Court` MEANS
    IF `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in months` AT MOST 6
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than an offence punishable with imprisonment for a term exceeding 6 months" is a scope limit with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

@ref s 409(3) (src:28157-28161)
GIVEN `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409(3) the proceedings may be prosecuted in a District Court` MEANS
    IF `the longest term of imprisonment the offence is punishable with, in months` AT LEAST 6
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an offence punishable with imprisonment for a term of 6 months or more"

-- src:28169 | (7) Any punishment authorised by this Act may be imposed by a
-- src:28170 | District Court, even though it is a greater punishment than that Court
-- src:28171 | is otherwise empowered to impose.
@ref s 409(7) (src:28169-28171)
GIVEN `the punishment is authorised by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409(7) a District Court may impose the punishment although it is greater than the Court is otherwise empowered to impose` MEANS
    IF `the punishment is authorised by this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any punishment authorised by this Act"

-- src:28173 | (8) The Registrar and any officer authorised by the Registrar in
-- src:28174 | writing has the right to appear and be heard before a Magistrate’s
-- src:28179 | Court or a District Court in any proceedings for an offence under this
-- src:28180 | Act.
@ref s 409(8) (src:28173-28180)
GIVEN `the person is the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer authorised by the Registrar in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409(8) the person has the right to appear and be heard before a Magistrate's Court or a District Court in proceedings for an offence under this Act` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Registrar` OR `the person is an officer authorised by the Registrar in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection gives the right to "The Registrar and any officer authorised by the Registrar in writing" and does not say that no one else has it

§ `Section 409B: composition of offences`

§§ `Section 409B(1): compounding an offence that is prescribed as compoundable`

-- "a sum of money not exceeding the lower of (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $20,000."
-- src:28273 | 409B.—(1) The Registrar may, in his or her discretion, compound
-- src:28274 | any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a compoundable
-- src:28275 | offence by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having
-- src:28276 | committed the offence a sum of money not exceeding the lower of the
-- src:28277 | following:
-- src:28279 | (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is
-- src:28280 | prescribed for the offence;
-- src:28282 | (b) $20,000.
@ref s 409B(1) (src:28273-28282)
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 409B(1) the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` AND `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence`
    THEN JUST (min (`the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence, in Singapore dollars` DIVIDED BY 2) 20000)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence"; which offences are prescribed is for the Minister (subsection (4)), outside the text

-- src:28288 | (2) The Registrar may, in his or her discretion, compound any
-- src:28289 | offence under this Act (including an offence under a provision that
-- src:28290 | has been repealed) which —
-- src:28292 | (a) was compoundable under this Act at the time the offence
-- src:28293 | was committed; but
-- src:28295 | (b) has ceased to be so compoundable,
-- src:28297 | by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having
-- src:28298 | committed the offence a sum of money not exceeding the lower of
-- src:28299 | the following:
-- src:28301 | (c) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is
-- src:28302 | prescribed for the offence at the time it was committed;
-- src:28304 | (d) $20,000.
@ref s 409B(2) (src:28288-28304)
GIVEN `the offence was compoundable under this Act at the time the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence has ceased to be so compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum fine that was prescribed for the offence at the time it was committed, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 409B(2) the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence that has ceased to be compoundable` MEANS
    IF    `the offence was compoundable under this Act at the time the offence was committed`
       AND `the offence has ceased to be so compoundable`
       AND `the person is reasonably suspected of having committed the offence`
    THEN JUST (min (`the maximum fine that was prescribed for the offence at the time it was committed, in Singapore dollars` DIVIDED BY 2) 20000)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "compound any offence ... which (a) was compoundable under this Act at the time the offence was committed; but (b) has ceased to be so compoundable"

-- src:28310 | (3) On payment of the sum of money referred to in subsection (1) or
-- src:28311 | (2), no further proceedings may be taken against that person in
-- src:28312 | respect of the offence.
@ref s 409B(3) (src:28310-28312)
GIVEN `the person has paid the sum of money referred to in section 409B(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409B(3) no further proceedings may be taken against the person in respect of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person has paid the sum of money referred to in section 409B(1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On payment of the sum of money referred to in subsection (1) or (2), no further proceedings may be taken"; the subsection says nothing of the person who has not paid

§ `First Schedule: repealed written laws (section 3(1))`

-- The table of the Schedule, three rows. Each row names a written law by its number in the 1955 Edition and gives the extent of the repeal.
DECLARE `sch 1 repealed written law` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 The Foreign Corporations (Execution of Instruments under Seal) Ordinance`
    `sch 1 The Companies Ordinance`
    `sch 1 The Companies (Special Provisions) Ordinance`

-- src:28485 | REPEALED WRITTEN LAWS Section 3(1)
-- src:28487 | Number in . Short Title . Extent of
-- src:28488 | 1955 Edition Repeal
-- src:28489 | The Foreign Corporations
-- src:28490 | Cap. 15 (Execution of Instruments under The whole.
-- src:28491 | Seal) Ordinance
-- src:28492 | Cap. 174 The Companies Ordinance The whole.
-- src:28493 | Cap. 277 The Companies (Special The whole.
-- src:28494 | Provisions) Ordinance
@ref sch 1 (src:28485-28494)
GIVEN law IS A `sch 1 repealed written law`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1 the number in the 1955 Edition` MEANS
    CONSIDER law
    WHEN `sch 1 The Foreign Corporations (Execution of Instruments under Seal) Ordinance` THEN 15
    WHEN `sch 1 The Companies Ordinance` THEN 174
    WHEN `sch 1 The Companies (Special Provisions) Ordinance` THEN 277

@ref sch 1 (src:28485-28494)
GIVEN law IS A `sch 1 repealed written law`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 1 the extent of the repeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER law
    WHEN `sch 1 The Foreign Corporations (Execution of Instruments under Seal) Ordinance` THEN "The whole."
    WHEN `sch 1 The Companies Ordinance` THEN "The whole."
    WHEN `sch 1 The Companies (Special Provisions) Ordinance` THEN "The whole."

-- Whether a written law is one of those the Schedule lists, asked by its 1955 Edition number. The Schedule lists three and does not say "only":
-- the repealing section (s 3(1), the keel) governs the rest, so a number the Schedule does not list answers NOTHING.
@ref sch 1 (src:28485-28494)
GIVEN `the number of the written law in the 1955 Edition` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 the written law is one of those the First Schedule lists` MEANS
    IF    `the number of the written law in the 1955 Edition` EQUALS 15
       OR `the number of the written law in the 1955 Edition` EQUALS 174
       OR `the number of the written law in the 1955 Edition` EQUALS 277
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the table lists three written laws and does not say "only"
